# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# Env & secrets
.env
.env.profile
.env.bak
.env.*.local

# Credentials and keys, by shape rather than by name. Nothing matching these has
# ever been committed here — the point is that nothing ever is, including the
# file someone drops in at 2am during an incident and forgets about.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.kdbx
secrets/
.secrets/

# Database dumps and embedded stores. A dump of this system's Postgres carries
# every account row and password hash; a `.duckdb` file is one tenant's whole
# vector index. Both are the kind of thing that gets written next to the code
# "just for a minute" during a restore.
*.sql
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Editor and tooling backups. `.env.bak` is already named above, but the same
# accident with any other name — `docker-compose.yml~`, `Caddyfile.orig` — puts
# a working copy of a real config in the repo.
*~
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp

# Personal / deployment-specific notes. This repo is public: the docs teach how
# to self-host the system, and nothing here should identify where *this* copy of
# it runs. Untracked alone isn't enough — one `git add .` publishes it.
ONBOARDING.md
NOTES.md
notes/

# Operational material for *this* deployment. None of it contains a secret, but
# together it describes the security posture of a specific running box — which
# ports are closed, what the SSH policy is, what is monitored and what is not.
# That is a map for someone probing the host, and it is worth exactly nothing to
# a reader who just wants to self-host the project. `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` stays
# public and covers everything they actually need.
docs/HARDENING.md
scripts/harden-host.sh

# Internal planning. Roadmaps read as commitments to people who find them.
docs/MULTI-AGENT-PLAN.md
docs/*-PLAN.md
TODO.md

# Data & models
# Ignore ingested/uploaded content, but ship the sample corpus the README's
# quickstart ingests — without it, `graphrag ingest data/sample.md` fails on a
# fresh clone — and the golden eval set that scores against it.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/sample.md
!data/eval/
!data/eval/**
models/
*.log

# Web apps. The lockfiles ARE tracked: `npm ci` (used by CI and by the proxy
# image build) needs them, and without one the image ships a dependency tree
# nobody tested.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
admin/node_modules/
admin/dist/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
scripts/harden-host.sh
docs/HARDENING.md
docs/MULTI-AGENT-PLAN.md
